{%- elsif key == 'faq' -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "Responsible Business Consulting FAQs | VECTRA International",
      "headline": "Responsible Business Consulting FAQs",
      "description": "Find answers about VECTRA International, responsible business consulting, supply chain consulting, business resilience, technology, and more.",
      "keywords": "Responsible business consulting FAQs, Supply chain consulting FAQs, Responsible business FAQs",
      "url": "{{ request.origin }}{{ page.url | default: '/pages/faq' }}",
      "about": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "VECTRA International", "url": "{{ shop.url }}" },
      "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "VECTRA International", "url": "{{ shop.url }}" }
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {"@type":"Question","name":"What is VECTRA International?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"VECTRA International is a business resilience and operational capability-building partner founded in 2005. Our work includes responsible business consulting, supplier and value-chain issues, risk, reporting, technology, operational improvement, and capability building. We help organizations turn identified issues into clearer ownership, practical action, stronger evidence, and changes that work in day-to-day operations."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Why work with VECTRA International?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"VECTRA International brings more than 20 years of experience, a network of 50+ global experts, and experience supporting 500+ organizations. More importantly, we stay close to what happens after the assessment, finding, or recommendation."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Is VECTRA International a global organization?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. VECTRA International works globally through a network of specialists and associates with experience across markets, industries, and value chains. Our office is in Brussels, Belgium, while project teams are built around the technical expertise and local context the work requires."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Where does VECTRA International work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"VECTRA International supports organizations and value chains globally. The exact team depends on the issue, operating context, and specialist knowledge required. We do not use one generalist team for every engagement."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Who does VECTRA International work with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"VECTRA International works with small and mid-sized businesses, global enterprises, industry groups, and value-chain partners. Client teams often include executive leadership, operations, procurement, supply chain, risk, compliance, sustainability, finance, quality, legal, and people functions."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"When should we bring VECTRA International into a business challenge?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Bring us in when you know something needs attention but the path forward is unclear, or when the same issue keeps returning despite previous action. That could be a supplier problem, recurring finding, weak evidence, unclear ownership, a new requirement, or a change that is not working as expected."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Can VECTRA International help with one specific problem?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. You can start with one defined issue or business outcome. The first piece of work can establish what is happening, what needs to change, and whether a wider response is actually necessary. A large program does not need to be the starting point."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Can VECTRA International work alongside our existing teams and advisors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We work with the people, systems, specialists, and partners already involved. The aim is to add the expertise, structure, or implementation support the work is missing without creating another disconnected layer around it."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"What if our challenge crosses several teams or functions?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"That is common. A supplier problem, for example, may involve procurement, operations, risk, evidence, remediation, and capability at the same time. VECTRA International can bring the relevant expertise around the same issue so the work does not get split into unrelated projects with different owners and priorities."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"What does business resilience mean in VECTRA International's work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Business resilience is the ability to keep important business outcomes under control as conditions change. In practice, that can mean understanding risk earlier, keeping ownership clear, strengthening suppliers and processes, having evidence people can trust, and making sure teams know how to respond when something changes."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"How is business resilience different from business continuity?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Business continuity focuses mainly on keeping critical activities running or restoring them after disruption. Business resilience is broader. It includes continuity, but also covers how the organization understands risk, manages suppliers, strengthens controls, uses evidence, builds capability, and adapts before, during, and after disruption."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"What is supply chain due diligence?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Supply chain due diligence is the process of identifying, assessing, prioritizing, and responding to risks connected to suppliers and other value-chain relationships. The useful part comes after the assessment: deciding what matters, who owns the response, and what action should follow."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Can VECTRA International work directly with suppliers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, where the engagement requires it. VECTRA International's supply chain consulting work can include direct engagement with suppliers on assessment, remediation, performance improvement, evidence, and capability alongside the client's procurement, operations, risk, compliance, or sustainability teams."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"What happens after a supplier risk is identified?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"First, determine how significant the issue is, who owns the response, and what needs to happen next. That may involve further assessment, mitigation, remediation, supplier improvement, stronger evidence, or follow-through over time. A risk score on its own does not close the issue."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"How can VECTRA International help improve supplier performance?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We look behind the recurring problem. The gap may sit in process, ownership, controls, communication, capability, or the way corrective actions are followed through. The aim is to understand what needs to change, make the action clear, and see whether the improvement holds after the immediate issue is closed."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Is VECTRA International a software or AI company?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. VECTRA International is a business resilience and operational capability-building partner. Technology and AI can support analysis, monitoring, workflows, and decision-making, but people remain responsible for interpreting the situation, deciding what matters, and carrying the response into practice."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"How does VECTRA International use AI?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We use AI where it can make information easier to analyze, highlight patterns, improve visibility, or support faster decisions. AI supports the work. Human judgment, business context, specialist knowledge, and accountability determine what the information means and what happens next."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Can VECTRA International work with the platforms and systems we already use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. VECTRA International is platform-agnostic. We start with what is already in place and look at where the real gap sits. If existing systems can support the work, we work with them. A new platform should only be introduced when it solves a clear problem."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"What if our data and evidence are spread across different systems?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"That is often less a technology problem than an ownership and control problem. VECTRA can help clarify which information matters, where it comes from, who owns it, how it is used, and where gaps affect decisions or evidence. The goal is to make existing information more useful before assuming another system is required."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Is ESG Consulting part of VECTRA International's work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. ESG Compliance and responsible business consulting are part of VECTRA International's work where they affect risk, suppliers, governance, reporting, evidence, market requirements, or operational performance."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Can VECTRA International help with sustainability reporting and disclosure?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We can help strengthen the work behind the report, including data ownership, evidence, internal review, disclosure readiness, and coordination between the teams responsible for producing and supporting the information."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"What is assurance and verification?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Assurance and verification provide an independent check on whether information, evidence, controls, or processes can be relied on. They help decision-makers understand what holds up, where gaps remain, and where stronger evidence or control is required."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Can VECTRA International strengthen the evidence behind our reporting or decisions?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We can help identify evidence gaps, clarify ownership, improve traceability, and strengthen the way information is collected, reviewed, and supported. The practical test is whether the people relying on that information can find it, trust it, and defend the decision it supports."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"How does capability building fit into VECTRA International's work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Capability building helps the people responsible for a change understand what is expected and apply it in their everyday work. It may support a wider engagement or address a focused knowledge or adoption gap for leaders, employees, suppliers, or other teams."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"What is VECTRA Marketplace?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"VECTRA Marketplace is VECTRA International's learning platform for practical courses across responsible business, supply chains, compliance, risk, governance, and related business needs. It gives individuals and teams a direct way to build knowledge where learning is the immediate need."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Is Marketplace training the same as a VECTRA International consulting or implementation engagement?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Marketplace is a learning route. A wider VECTRA International engagement starts with a defined business problem and may involve assessment, specialist expertise, process improvement, implementation, assurance, supplier work, or capability building. The two can work together when stronger knowledge is part of solving the business problem."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Do we need a finished scope before contacting VECTRA International?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Start with the issue, recurring problem, requirement, or business result that needs attention. A first conversation can help clarify where the gap sits and what kind of support makes sense next."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Can we start with one area and expand later?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Starting with one clearly defined issue can make priorities, ownership, and progress easier to see. If the work later points to a broader need, you can decide what comes next from a clearer baseline instead of starting with a program larger than the problem requires."}}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
</script>
